# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Next.js and the registry scripts read it; .env.local is gitignored.

# The site's origin with no trailing slash, such as https://kosmosui.com. Metadata, the sitemap, robots.txt,
# llms.txt, the .md pages and every install command (the registry URL) are built from it.
# On Vercel it falls back to the production URL; elsewhere, unset, everything publishes localhost.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# The origin of the Pro deployment (the private kosmos-pro app) with no trailing slash, such as https://pro.kosmosui.com.
# The Blocks pages show each Pro variant live in an iframe from it, with a Pro badge and its code locked, and the
# sidebar counts and the landing include them. Unset, the site shows no Pro variant and nothing else changes.
# In development, run kosmos-pro on its own port and set http://localhost:<port>.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KOSMOS_PRO_URL=
